      "side": 1,
      "message": "While I am not a fan of going away from UUID, I think 16 bytes is a bit too restrictive limitation. Personally I think the name should follow java-like package naming scheme if readability is the reason for this. Eg. `com.google.android.virt.trusty` and such. Because multiple vendors might want to run a similarily named VM.\n\nSide note: our AP firmware has to be updated anyway to reflect this change anyway already, so if it were a reaon for 16-bytes I think it doesn\u0027t have to be 😅",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 10,
