      "writtenOn": "2025-02-12T10:29:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, the main reason for this is to be able to use the name as the (already existing) `component_name` in the DICE chain, which gets recognized by our servers in the context of remote attestation. I don\u0027t want to have 2 different (potentially conflicting) identifiers for almost the same purpose. FWIW, I would also favor the UUID format given the choice.\n\n\u003e  I think the name should follow java-like package naming scheme if readability is the reason for this\n\nGood point!\n\nAs it isn\u0027t directly blocking this CL, let\u0027s discuss it elsewhere; see b/390527025#comment11.\n\n\u003e Because multiple vendors might want to run a similarily named VM.\n\nFYI, the DICE authority would also reflect that (in theory).\n\n\u003e so if it were a reaon for 16-bytes I think it doesn\u0027t have to be\n\nAh! Good to know and thanks for pointing this out!\n\nYes, that was the reason for this limitation.\n\nThen, let\u0027s update the format (b/382493676#comment8) and I\u0027ll relax this.",
